  "verdict": "two-prior-open-findings-source-closed-no-confirmed-remaining-source-blocker-in-reviewed-delta",
  "confirmedRemainingBlockers": [],
  "confirmedClosures": [
    {
      "id": "batch-cleanup-io-is-not-invalidity",
      "source": "Modules/Services/Online/ChapterCacheRepository.swift:130-190;764-802",
      "facts": [
        "onlyIfInvalid now calls the actual owner bounded throwing FD reader for every companion. Only true ENOENT yields absence; open/pread/fstat/identity/size/close/observed-change failures throw before granting deletion.",
        "Only explicit empty/non-UTF8 body, missing required body with other artifacts, actual DecodingError, checksum mismatch, noncached state or original content rejection authorizes invalidity cleanup. Unknown I/O never becomes compatibility-loader nil and permission failure preserves original files.",
        "The existing compatibility loader may still be used to refuse a mismatched expected-package cleanup; its nil in that branch only refuses deletion. No new queue, cache or ordinary reader path is created.",
        "Existing real-file regression now changes the actual body mode to000, awaits the actual clear API expecting an error, restores permissions and compares all actual prior artifact bytes. Definition only; no macOS/SDK execution was performed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "batch-variable-commit-missing-effect-seal",
      "source": "LegadoPersistentStateHost -> existing entity backing -> actual BookStore/BookChapterStore/preview writer",
      "facts": [
        "Original request.recordPossibleEffect claim is passed through every actual entity owner into the point preceding the real metadata/chapter atomic write. Sealed requests refuse before issuing that write.",
        "The existing Native callback closePossibleEffects uses the same recorder lock as the claim. A write admitted before timeout therefore retains conservative bookVariablesMayCommit or chapterVariablesMayCommit; a later ticket cancellation cannot erase it. A completed write can additionally record Committed while the callback remains open.",
        "BookStore accepts its actual metadata proof and invokes its accepted observer only after real write, on the same persistence queue. Chapter owner publishes its accepted revision only after the actual writer; failed or denied claim keeps previous visible/durable state.",
        "The shared preview adapter forwards the same claim into its existing preview owner before replacement. Its later cancellation check may still prevent a claimed write; that is an honest conservative MayCommit rather than an invented success.",
        "Read the existing per-owner same-entity key guards, all new protocol conformances/callers, callback seal implementation and three expanded production-owner tests. No alternate state/queue/authority flag is introduced. Native/Keychain/JNI behavior remains unexecuted."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "reviewScope": "Read the complete v2-to-v3 diff; inspected actual strict FD reader, BookStore/chapter atomic writes/acceptance, preview replacement/write/parse, Host entity lease and claim path, exact recorder/timeout lock, and changed real-file/denied-claim definitions. Prior relevant all-writer/TOC/cache/direct-book CAS review remains the earlier independent report. This is not a line-by-line review of unrelated whole BookStore/UI files.",
  "withdrawnReviewSuspicion": {
    "topic": "Mixed preview entity keys",
    "fact": "Root initially read a truncated parse excerpt and suspected a missing same-entity guard. Author pointed to the existing guard; root reread frozen v3 lines264-284 and confirmed all keys must match first.chapterURL. The suspicion was withdrawn without a production change or invented test pass."
